# WealthWise AI Response System — Todo List

## Architecture & Existing System

* [x] Inspect the existing Next.js chat architecture and current message rendering flow.
* [x] Inspect how the Django backend communicates with the ML/AI backend and Ollama.
* [x] Review the existing Alerts and Insights tools/agents and how their data is retrieved.
* [x] Review the current chat/message database models and persistence logic.
* [x] Review existing logging, error handling, and streaming implementation.
* [x] Reuse existing APIs, models, utilities, and infrastructure wherever practical instead of creating duplicates.

## Structured AI Response Pipeline

* [x] Change the AI pipeline so financial responses are returned as structured data instead of relying primarily on free-form Markdown.
* [x] Define a consistent response schema that can represent financial insights, metrics, tables, alerts, recommendations, charts, tool results, text, and errors.
* [x] Validate every structured Ollama response before sending it to the frontend.
* [x] Keep the schema extensible so new response types can be added without redesigning the whole system.
* [x] Separate data/content decisions made by the AI from presentation decisions made by Next.js.
* [x] Ensure Ollama never generates HTML, React components, CSS/Tailwind classes, or chart implementation code.

## Response Types

* [x] Support basic text and Markdown responses.
* [x] Support headings and structured sections.
* [x] Support individual metrics and groups of financial metrics.
* [x] Support general financial tables.
* [x] Support transaction-specific tables.
* [x] Support alerts and insights.
* [x] Support recommendations.
* [x] Support charts using structured data.
* [x] Support tool-result components.
* [x] Support error responses.
* [x] Keep the response-type system modular so additional components can be introduced later.

## Next.js Rendering

* [x] Create a centralized AI response renderer, such as `AIResponseRenderer.tsx`.
* [x] Make the renderer determine which UI component should be used for each response type.
* [x] Create separate reusable components for metrics, tables, transactions, alerts, insights, charts, Markdown, tool results, and errors.
* [x] Avoid creating one large renderer component containing all UI logic.
* [x] Make the renderer reusable across both the chat sidebar and dedicated `/chat` page.
* [x] Ensure structured responses render consistently after page refresh or when loading older conversations.

## Markdown Support

* [x] Add or standardize `react-markdown` with `remark-gfm`.
* [x] Properly render headings, bold text, italic text, lists, links, code, blockquotes, and tables.
* [x] Fix the existing Markdown table rendering problem.
* [x] Keep Markdown as a fallback for normal conversational responses that do not require structured financial components.
* [x] Prevent raw Markdown/JSON from being displayed when a structured component is available.

## Financial Tables

* [x] Represent financial tables as structured columns and rows rather than raw Markdown whenever possible.
* [x] Create a reusable responsive table component.
* [x] Handle currency, percentage, dates, categories, and other financial values consistently.
* [x] Make tables usable on small screens through horizontal scrolling or another suitable responsive layout.
* [x] Ensure large values do not break table layouts.

## Charts

* [x] Add a mature Next.js-compatible charting solution such as Recharts.
* [x] Allow the AI to return chart type and structured data only.
* [x] Keep chart implementation entirely on the frontend.
* [x] Create a reusable `ChartRenderer`.
* [x] Support common financial visualizations such as pie/donut, bar, and line charts where appropriate.
* [x] Only display charts when the returned data is meaningful for visualization.
* [x] Handle invalid or incomplete chart data gracefully.

## Number & Financial Formatting

* [x] Create one shared financial number-formatting utility.
* [x] Support currency, percentage, decimal, integer, and compact-number formats.
* [x] Support Indian financial notation such as ₹1,25,000, ₹12.5L, and ₹1.25Cr.
* [x] Define consistent rules for K, L, M, and Cr formatting.
* [x] Reuse the formatter across metrics, tables, charts, alerts, insights, and transaction views.
* [x] Avoid implementing separate number-formatting logic inside individual components.

## Database & Persistence

* [x] Review the existing database and determine the cleanest way to persist structured conversations.
* [x] Avoid storing the entire AI response only as one large text blob.
* [x] Store chats with user ownership and timestamps.
* [x] Store messages with role and ordering information.
* [x] Store individual message parts with their type, order, text, and structured data.
* [x] Store structured tool execution information separately where appropriate.
* [x] Prefer the existing project database instead of introducing another database unnecessarily.
* [x] Use JSON/JSONB for flexible structured AI and tool data where supported.
* [x] Ensure old conversations can be reconstructed accurately from stored data.

## Tool Execution History

* [x] Persist every AI tool execution.
* [x] Store tool name, input, output, status, execution duration, timestamp, and errors.
* [x] Make tool history associated with the relevant chat/message.
* [x] Ensure tool execution history can be used when reconstructing previous conversations.
* [x] Make the system ready for future tools such as Transactions, Budgets, Expenses, Income, Forecasts, Categories, and Accounts.

