## Transaction Support

* [x] Ensure the architecture supports a transaction-query tool.
* [x] Allow the agent to identify transaction-related requests and call the appropriate tool.
* [x] Return transaction results in structured form.
* [x] Create a reusable transaction table renderer.
* [x] Support fields such as date, merchant, amount, category, and other relevant transaction information.
* [x] Make transaction results persist and reload correctly with the conversation.

## Logging & Observability

* [x] Add useful logging across the complete AI pipeline.
* [x] Log major stages such as query reception, agent processing, tool selection, tool execution, Ollama request/response, validation, parsing, rendering, and completion.
* [x] Include enough information to identify where failures occur.
* [x] Add appropriate error logs for tool, parsing, validation, database, and Ollama failures.
* [x] Never log passwords, authentication tokens, API secrets, or private credentials.
* [x] Keep logs useful for debugging production issues without exposing sensitive financial information unnecessarily.

## Error Handling & Recovery

* [x] Make Ollama response parsing safe and fault tolerant.
* [x] Validate structured responses against the defined schema.
* [x] Handle malformed JSON without crashing the chat UI.
* [x] Add a controlled repair/retry mechanism for recoverable malformed responses.
* [x] Fall back to safe text/Markdown rendering if structured parsing cannot be recovered.
* [x] Log the original failure stage and reason.
* [x] Ensure invalid tool responses or chart/table data cannot crash the frontend.

## Streaming & Performance

* [x] Preserve the existing streaming experience where possible.
* [x] Avoid blocking the entire chat UI while large AI responses are being processed.
* [x] Determine how structured responses can be progressively delivered or rendered where practical.
* [x] Avoid unnecessary API calls, duplicate tool executions, or unnecessary database queries.
* [x] Keep the response pipeline efficient enough for normal interactive chat usage.

